"""A contextual 'more/much' signal and an opposing period--dash signal.

'More' is strongest after prepositions and 'a', weaker after copulas and
quantity modifiers. Lowercase rules apply to space-prefixed tokens.
'Much' is strong except in phrases such as 'how much',
'so much' and 'too much'. Period followed by dash is strongly negative;
ordinary dashes are not. Chinese comparative words get a smaller positive
response. Repeated middle-dot tokens are positive. Everything else is zero;
in particular this omits the component's scattered code-name responses.
